From: Abhi Teja Cholleti <achollet@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 25 Aug 2026
Subject: [PATCH] pwhm: fix wifi8 interface up issue with mldunit=-1

When a VAP has no MLD unit (mldunit=-1, non-MLO mode), hostapd needs
both disable_11be=1 and disable_11bn=1 to correctly disable Wi-Fi 7
(EHT) and Wi-Fi 8 (UHR/11bn) capabilities. Without disable_11bn=1,
the VAP may attempt to advertise 11bn capabilities even when MLO is
not configured, causing interface bring-up failures on wifi8 hardware.

Signed-off-by: Abhi Teja Cholleti <achollet@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_cfgFile.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_cfgFile.c
+++ b/src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_cfgFile.c
@@ -1486,6 +1486,7 @@
         } else {
             /* if no MLO, then no 11BE */
             swl_mapCharFmt_addValInt32(vapConfigMap, "disable_11be", 1);
+            swl_mapCharFmt_addValInt32(vapConfigMap, "disable_11bn", 1);
             swl_mapCharFmt_addValInt32(vapConfigMap, "mld_ap", 0);
             s_checkAndSetParamValueInt32(pAP->wpaCtrlInterface, vapConfigMap, "ttlm_enable", 0);
             enableVap11be = false;
